WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.209 --> 00:00:04.338
♪♪Wolf, Wolf, hunting far and
yonder♪♪

00:00:04.338 --> 00:00:05.839
♪♪

00:00:05.839 --> 00:00:08.008
Bill:
The forest is brimming with
wolves.

00:00:08.008 --> 00:00:10.052
Bill:
It's my job to hunt them
down, not yours.

00:00:10.052 --> 00:00:11.220
But we can hunt them together.

00:00:11.220 --> 00:00:13.430
Wolves, bears, dragons even!

00:00:13.430 --> 00:00:15.265
♪♪

00:00:15.265 --> 00:00:20.312
Cartoon Saloon, they make these
profoundly human films.

00:00:20.312 --> 00:00:22.314
Very beautiful, very poetic
films.

00:00:22.314 --> 00:00:24.149
♪♪

00:00:24.149 --> 00:00:25.275
Something's happened to me.

00:00:25.275 --> 00:00:26.777
I'm a wolfwalker!

00:00:26.777 --> 00:00:28.612
Yeah, it's flippin' great!

00:00:28.612 --> 00:00:32.658
You have four legs now, you can
run really fast and jump so
high!

00:00:32.658 --> 00:00:36.370
Simon McBurney:
And in this film the natural
world and the human world

00:00:36.370 --> 00:00:39.831
Simon McBurney:
are interconnected always as
people become animals

00:00:39.831 --> 00:00:41.375
Simon McBurney:
and animals become people.

00:00:41.375 --> 00:00:52.970
♪♪

00:00:52.970 --> 00:00:55.847
Ross Stewart:
Cromwellian Ireland is a
fascinating period in Irish history.

00:00:55.847 --> 00:00:59.351
Ross Stewart:
Cromwell is like the baddest
villian in Irish history

00:00:59.351 --> 00:01:00.352
if you ask most Irish people.

00:01:00.352 --> 00:01:01.353
♪♪

00:01:01.353 --> 00:01:04.106
Cromwell:
I want all the wolves gone from
this forest.

00:01:04.106 --> 00:01:05.107
Bill:
Yes, my lord.

00:01:05.107 --> 00:01:06.817
Goodefellow, you have two days.

00:01:06.817 --> 00:01:09.736
Ross Stewart:
Funny enough, he's the hero to a
lot of English people.

00:01:09.736 --> 00:01:12.531
Towns people:
Kill the wolf!

00:01:12.531 --> 00:01:16.159
That's when we had the idea of
two kids, one from England and
one from Ireland.

00:01:16.159 --> 00:01:19.997
I'm a wolfwalker, when I sleeps
I'm a wolf!

00:01:20.455 --> 00:01:22.958
When I'm awake, I'm me: Mebh.

00:01:22.958 --> 00:01:24.960
Mebh Óg MacTíre!

00:01:25.502 --> 00:01:26.503
What's your name, anyway?

00:01:27.337 --> 00:01:28.338
Robin.

00:01:28.338 --> 00:01:29.339
♪♪

00:01:29.339 --> 00:01:33.343
Our two main characters, Robin
and Mebh, actually seem very
different.

00:01:33.343 --> 00:01:34.428
♪♪

00:01:34.428 --> 00:01:36.847
Svend Bond:
Robin would be a lot more subtle
in her movements,

00:01:36.847 --> 00:01:38.557
Svend Bond:
a little bit more dainty.

00:01:38.557 --> 00:01:40.559
Svend Bond:
And Mebh is a little bit more
broad.

00:01:41.268 --> 00:01:42.728
Shhh, do you hear that?

00:01:42.728 --> 00:01:44.229
Robin muffled:
What?
(Mebh belches)

00:01:44.229 --> 00:01:45.605
♪♪

00:01:45.605 --> 00:01:48.942
Svend Bond:
The thing that made the
animation unique for this

00:01:48.942 --> 00:01:52.279
Svend Bond:
production I felt was that there
was a lot of focus on making

00:01:52.279 --> 00:01:56.074
Svend Bond:
things seem very natural and
keeping the lines more loose.

00:01:56.074 --> 00:01:59.870
♪♪

00:01:59.870 --> 00:02:02.789
Svend Bond:
So for us in rough animation we
could be a little more free.

00:02:02.789 --> 00:02:04.916
Robin:
You can't stay in the forest,
they're cutting it all down.

00:02:04.916 --> 00:02:07.085
No way, I scare them off!

00:02:07.085 --> 00:02:09.755
(Mebh howling like a wolf)

00:02:09.755 --> 00:02:16.094
♪♪

00:02:16.094 --> 00:02:18.680
The style that we were aiming
for was extremely high.

00:02:18.680 --> 00:02:20.974
♪♪

00:02:20.974 --> 00:02:24.227
Helga Bjarnadóttir:
We developed a way of offsetting
the colors outside of the lines

00:02:24.227 --> 00:02:26.605
Helga Bjarnadóttir:
to make it look like mistakes
and wood-block printing.

00:02:26.605 --> 00:02:31.735
♪♪

00:02:31.735 --> 00:02:33.945
Helga Bjarnadóttir:
The forest line was quite
difficult to color.

00:02:33.945 --> 00:02:36.281
♪♪

00:02:36.281 --> 00:02:39.576
Helga Bjarnadóttir:
We developed a style to kind of
make the outside of the color

00:02:39.576 --> 00:02:41.995
Helga Bjarnadóttir:
shapes a bit fuzzy, to look
like watercolor.

00:02:41.995 --> 00:02:45.457
♪♪

00:02:45.457 --> 00:02:47.876
Helga Bjarnadóttir:
We had to do quite a lot by
hand, which took longer.

00:02:48.335 --> 00:02:49.753
But in the end it looks
beautiful.

00:02:49.753 --> 00:02:52.881
♪♪

00:02:52.881 --> 00:02:56.968
In this film, there is this very
interesting relationship with
nature.

00:02:56.968 --> 00:03:00.514
Simon McBurney:
In which flows into the human
world and back out again.

00:03:00.889 --> 00:03:02.349
Mebh:
Why'd you want to be human?

00:03:02.349 --> 00:03:05.352
Being a wolf is way better, I'll
show ya.

00:03:05.352 --> 00:03:08.522
♪♪

00:03:08.522 --> 00:03:11.900
Simon McBurney:
The amazing thing of working
with Cartoon Saloon,

00:03:11.900 --> 00:03:15.028
other than the beautiful
animation and the stories...

00:03:15.028 --> 00:03:16.363
Smell ya later, Townie.

00:03:16.363 --> 00:03:19.074
...is the fact that something
touches us.

00:03:19.074 --> 00:03:24.287
♪♪

